WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.650
Purple heather across an open upland moor.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:06.490
Cottongrass over a blanket bog.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.110
Blanket bogs stretch from Devon in
the south to Shetland in the north.

4
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.350
Yet most of them sit in
the UK's north and west.

5
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.950
In the lowlands of south
and central England,

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.770
heath is more patchy.

7
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.890
So why do moors and bogs crowd
into the north and the west?

8
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:23.530
Is it the cold?

9
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.730
Or the grouse estates?

10
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.690
In this mission, you'll meet
four UK land ecosystems:

11
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.910
moorland, heath, woodland and wetland.

12
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:39.590
Then you'll head offshore, and weigh
how people use and damage the UK's seas.

13
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.590
Your mission: explain where the
UK's moors and bogs grow, and why.
